From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:43:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] clef: Cloudflare's joint decision head on a Qwen3.5 trunk,
 from ggml-org #29831 (arch, decision order, converter, test)

Ported from ggml-org/llama.cpp PR 29831 (99b95488ca, merged 2026-10-03, MIT), text only, onto the tree of patch 0048.

- arch "clef" (src/models/clef.cpp): the Qwen3.5 trunk evaluated WITHOUT memory (llama_model_clef::create_memory is null: the
  gated-delta-net layers start from a zero state and keep none, the attention layers are causal over the batch), then the
  head: routing blocks and joint blocks of cross/self attention over the prompt, pooled spans of question and option
  tokens, a prior from the output embeddings, a scorer; the embeddings output has one score per option, row i = option i.
  Tensors, KVs (clef.decision.block_count, routing_block_count, head_count), the head's widths read from the file, the
  create_tensor() fix for blocks past the model's layers.
- the order of the tokens: PR 29831 adds llama_batch_ext_set_decision_order(), and this tree has no llama_batch_ext. The value
  rides in a trailing optional field of llama_batch (decision_order, NULL = none; include/llama.h) and of llama_ubatch,
  kept by llama_batch_allocr only when some token has one; enum llama_decision_order is in src/llama-ext.h as in the PR.
  A batch whose order cannot be used (an option before any question, a question without an option) scores NaN, which the
  server turns into an error. The server renders the order with the batch (server_batch) and never batches a clef task with
  another.
- server: fill_task_joint() puts all the questions of a request in ONE prompt (the "systemone" template the converter writes,
  pieces tokenized one by one as in training), is_joint(), choice options sorted by key, the scores read from the first
  rows of the embeddings. A server that runs clef serves /v1/systemone only; the prompt must fit in --ubatch-size.
- conversion/clef.py (ClefModel: the checkpoint's joint_head.safetensors, nn.MultiheadAttention's in_proj split into q/k/v,
  the learned scalars stored as the values used at inference), gguf-py constants, tensor map, writer methods.
- tests/test-clef.cpp (ctest): a tiny random clef GGUF built in the test (a qwen35 trunk saved by the model saver plus the
  head), 11 checks: finite and reproducible scores, they move with an option's or a question's tokens and with the order,
  NaN for an unusable order. Dump mode (--save, MODEL IN OUT) feeds bench/clef_smoke.py, which converts a tiny
  transformers Qwen3.5 + head checkpoint with this converter and compares the scores with a PyTorch reference:
  max |diff| 2.2e-4 on the CPU (float32). test-llama-archs skips the arch (the head tensors are not saved).

Not taken: llama_batch_ext, vision (PR 29969 and the mtmd entries PR 29622 would bring), the nimble model, the dsv4 KV cache
hunk (a one-line initializer, here for llama_ubatch's new field).

NOT RUN ON A GPU: the ggml graph is backend-neutral (mul_mat, norms, softmax, get_rows, gelu_erf, l2_norm), but the CUDA
build of the trunk's gated-delta-net layers (patch 0006, the fused op) has only run the QWEN35 memory path. The trunk here
passes zero states through build_delta_net() and keeps none.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
